ProtonPlus 0.6.0 declares the CpuFeatureProbe struct in Vala with both
[CCode(cname)] and [CCode(cheader_filename="utils/cpu-probe.h")]. valac
then emits the full struct body in the generated system.c AND #includes
cpu-probe.h, whose typedef defines the same struct -- gcc errors with
'redefinition of struct _ProtonPlusCpuFeatureProbe'.

Drop the cheader_filename from both the struct and the extern
get_cpu_feature_probe() declarations so valac emits its own struct and
its own extern prototype (matching the symbol provided by cpu-probe.c).
The generated struct layout is byte-identical to the header's.

Fixes: build failure in ProtonPlus 0.6.0 with vala 0.56.19

--- a/src/utils/system.vala
+++ b/src/utils/system.vala
@@ -208,7 +208,7 @@
         static bool systemd_update_pending = false;
         static SystemdTimerManager? systemd_timer_manager = null;
 
-        [CCode (cname = "ProtonPlusCpuFeatureProbe", cheader_filename = "utils/cpu-probe.h", has_type_id = false)]
+        [CCode (cname = "ProtonPlusCpuFeatureProbe", has_type_id = false)]
         private struct CpuFeatureProbe {
             public bool available;
             public bool cmpxchg16b;
@@ -242,7 +242,7 @@
             public bool aarch64_rdma;
         }
 
-        [CCode (cname = "protonplus_cpu_get_feature_probe", cheader_filename = "utils/cpu-probe.h", has_target = false)]
+        [CCode (cname = "protonplus_cpu_get_feature_probe", has_target = false)]
         private static extern CpuFeatureProbe get_cpu_feature_probe ();
 
         public static async CommandResult run_command (string command) {
